<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Title of your first post — Stanley Huang</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --text: #1a1a1a;
    --muted: #6a6a6a;
    --link: #0b5cad;
    --rule: #e4e4e4;
    --bg: #ffffff;
    --content-max: 720px;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }

  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font: 16px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }

  a { color: var(--link); text-decoration: none; }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--link); outline-offset: 2px; border-radius: 2px; }

  /* A post is a single centered column — no sidebar, so the text leads. */
  .post-wrap {
    max-width: var(--content-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 56px 28px 80px;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .post-header { margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .post-header h1 {
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 27px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0 0 6px;
  }
  .post-header .meta {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  article p { margin: 0 0 18px; }
  article h2 {
    font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 36px 0 12px;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  article blockquote {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding-left: 16px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  article img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 3px; }
  article figure { margin: 24px 0; }
  article figcaption { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  article code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 14px;
    background: #f5f5f5;
    padding: 1px 4px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  article pre {
    background: #f5f5f5;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  article pre code { background: none; padding: 0; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .post-wrap { padding: 32px 20px 56px; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    * { scroll-behavior: auto !important; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="post-wrap">

    <a class="back" href="../blog.html">&larr; All posts</a>

    <header class="post-header">
      <h1>Title of your first post</h1>
      <p class="meta">January 4, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <article>
      <p>
        Open with the point. A blog post earns attention faster than a paper does,
        so say in the first paragraph what you found, argued, or built.
      </p>

      <h2>A section heading</h2>
      <p>
        Ordinary paragraphs go here. You can use <a href="#">links</a>,
        <em>emphasis</em>, <strong>bold</strong>, and <code>inline code</code>.
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        A pull quote or a quotation from something you are responding to.
      </blockquote>

      <figure>
        <img src="../me.jpg" alt="Describe the image for screen readers">
        <figcaption>A caption explaining what the figure shows.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <pre><code>// a code block, if you need one
print("hello")</code></pre>

      <h2>Closing</h2>
      <p>
        End with what you are still unsure about, or what you plan to do next.
      </p>
    </article>

  </div>
</body>
</html>
